{"title":"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(video_solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (video solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Very_similar_to_solution_2_but_explained_more)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Very similar to solution 2 but explained more)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(graphical)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (graphical)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Without_similar_triangles)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Without similar triangles)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Trivia\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Trivia</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A right circular cylinder with its diameter equal to its height is inscribed in a right circular cone. The cone has diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and altitude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and the axes of the cylinder and cone coincide. Find the radius of the cylinder. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/8/f1865b40e1bdd0d0ac7d74f4f60fc0cb13fe0806.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{8}3\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{30}{11}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 3\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{25}{8}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{7}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"382\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28video_solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(video_solution)\">Solution 1 (video solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (video solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/HUM035eNKvU\">https://youtu.be/HUM035eNKvU</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/4/8a48ba1b569474a4227381a6d073567c8d68ddf3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((5,0)--(-5,0)--(0,12)--cycle); unitsize(.75cm); draw((-30/11,0)--(-30/11,60/11)); draw((-30/11,60/11)--(30/11,60/11)); draw((30/11,60/11)--(30/11,0)); draw((0,0)--(0,12)); label(&quot;$2r$&quot;,(0,30/11),E); label(&quot;$12-2r$&quot;,(0,80/11),E); label(&quot;$2r$&quot;,(0,60/11),S); label(&quot;$10$&quot;,(0,0),S); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(0,12),N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(-5,0),SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(5,0),SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,(-30/11,60/11),W); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,(30/11,60/11),E);     [/asy]\" width=\"402\" height=\"472\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\nLet the diameter of the cylinder be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/5/0a5745df50c8607bdc9b8de4968315633a3047dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2r$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />. Examining the cross section of the cone and cylinder, we find two similar triangles. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/7/557851c71192cdfe529469db4cb1eb483f4a871e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{12-2r}{12}=\\frac{2r}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"107\" height=\"37\" /> which we solve to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/e/72e542a1cd3873274873bf2c4b8f988b0dc57643.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\frac{30}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"53\" height=\"38\" />. Our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/1/ad1415f179cda5ba534a08c1e91bc83393dc988f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{30}{11}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"69\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Very_similar_to_solution_2_but_explained_more.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Very_similar_to_solution_2_but_explained_more)\">Solution 3 (Very similar to solution 2 but explained more)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Very similar to solution 2 but explained more)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are asked to find the radius of the cylinder, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> so we can look for similarity. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/e/14eabe8a33f60df9e8c23bb4fc729309b9f47a8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BEF = \\angle BDA$\" width=\"137\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/d/bbd19a8ba2d9691779df3a30e767da5dcb283bd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FBE = \\angle ABD$\" width=\"136\" height=\"13\" />, thus we have similarity between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/0/f00afb3996c4aa5426ec79a3d7334010023053d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BFE$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/6/1661ac6f3544a6f06f111d5e09c7072da8bb76e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BAD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/b/b0b3dbb5e0c16cabfa02f10ace626714ac385dbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AA$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> similarity. \n</p><p>Therefore, we can create an equation to find the length of the desired side. We know that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/3/1e38cdb2bc4e9ccc815218af0be3b652edef18ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BE}{BD}=\\frac{FE}{AD}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"95\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><br />\nPlugging in yields:\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/e/c4e70f3a49418126aed017bdf8af4097f25856f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{12-2r}{12}=\\frac{r}{5}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"103\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Cross multiplying and simplifying gives:\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/d/03d73d2cbfb096a1466615a503fd6c84a6b5d035.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5(12-2r)=12r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd90d68c14531a18fb1309c26d5cb62e9216da54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Downarrow$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/d/e9d7314f3d7ec265b095e879cb076a7e8848bb7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\frac{30}{11}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"58\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Since the problem asks us to find the radius of the cylinder, we are done and the radius of the cylinder is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/1/ad1415f179cda5ba534a08c1e91bc83393dc988f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{30}{11}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"69\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~etvat\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28graphical.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(graphical)\">Solution 4 (graphical)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (graphical)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Assume that a point on a given diameter of the cone is the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> on a two-dimensional representation of the cone as shown in Solution 2. The top point of the cone is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/2/372b122f51cad9f701b1d946b28c2f07f55c18de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5,12)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> and the line that goes through both points is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/2/c822317ff6a16c5c6dc622bff839e1862f7d4088.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{12}{5}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Now we create a second equation. We must choose some point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> on the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/2/c822317ff6a16c5c6dc622bff839e1862f7d4088.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{12}{5}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/1/2a1c95a0cfd6b8f36e657f5a2d9fe7c24e4e9aed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=10-2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"17\" />, which implies that the cylinder’s diameter, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/c/06c7eb522571ef248e9f1f9eab3e1c59e6424dd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10-2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />, must be equal to its height, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Solving yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/3/ae3eb049588d4cc038e55ea45d9b24e115ad3623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{25}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"38\" />, and the radius is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/8/e98a5c95046c6d3a1965f036447dc79778cff46d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{10-2x}{2}=\\frac{\\frac{60}{11}}{2}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{30}{11}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"203\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Without_similar_triangles.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Without_similar_triangles)\">Solution 5 (Without similar triangles)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Without similar triangles)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like in Solution 2, we draw a diagram.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/6/df6073c7c71ab7b2b4c1ac02b5dba65855f16c3d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((5,0)--(-5,0)--(0,12)--cycle); unitsize(.75cm); draw((-30/11,0)--(-30/11,60/11)); draw((-30/11,60/11)--(30/11,60/11)); draw((30/11,60/11)--(30/11,0)); draw((0,0)--(0,12)); label(&quot;$2x$&quot;,(0,30/11),E); label(&quot;$2x$&quot;,(0,60/11),S); label(&quot;$H$&quot;,(0,0),S); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(0,12),N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(-5,0),SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(5,0),SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,(-30/11,60/11),W); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,(30/11,60/11),E); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,(30/11,0),S); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,(-30/11,0),S); [/asy]\" width=\"402\" height=\"472\" />\n</p><p>It is known that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/0/5605e7674254425ca5932c0a752f8a04b6b16770.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AH}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Also, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be equal to the radius of the cylinder.\n</p><p><br />\nTriangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/8/6787229ba3ecf14232de4b1efeac6b4617f413f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DBG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/1/f71fa1f1024c0df6b157160c35276942c4b63eb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ECF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> can be combined into one triangle with base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/c/06c7eb522571ef248e9f1f9eab3e1c59e6424dd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10-2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />. The area of this new triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/5/6655abd45de41ff023138a9743b500feb32cbd31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2x(10-2x)}{2} = 2x(5-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"199\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/0/db041d9c0fda44cf24b4f4ae7f02243ef2ea7f92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADE$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> has base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/c/c3c572fb9ad99cdbfc544ce30e59bed2dfab6f62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12-2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" />, so its area is<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/f/c0fa4320759f1291623d1038c4c6fb3b4da38a03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2x(12-2x)}{2} = 2x(6-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"199\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>Finally, square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16df895dad08efcc67a9a5d66f8eb08a7c37e8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEFG$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/7/4675e27bb11d6efd975189436e433aaaf1677af2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nNow we can construct an equation to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/7/d87184921afde666c0395c6d61a8ed2b019b330b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2x(5-x) + 2x(6-x) + 4x^2 = 60\\]\" width=\"263\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/1/221891b1417153cb36756f5246aaef7995691813.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Rightarrow 2x(5-x+6-x+2x) = 60\\]\" width=\"245\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/3/3035b53a32522078de901d8da351f0b4599ef836.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Rightarrow 2x(11) = 60\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/80293d70668a219aa6f97c2fbb28039651a3bb60.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Rightarrow 22x = 60\\]\" width=\"93\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/2/fd2ebb8b34948488ade3e7eec12efc84085af8b7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Rightarrow x = \\frac{60}{22} = \\boxed{(B) \\frac{30}{11}}\\]\" width=\"166\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>~Dreamer1297\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Trivia\">Trivia</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Trivia\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This problem appeared in AoPS's Introduction to Geometry as a challenge problem.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10\" title=\"2001 AMC 10\">2001 AMC 10</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Answer_Key\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href